<div style="width: 100%; background-color: #1a5276; padding: 20px; color: white; text-align: center; border-radius: 8px;">
    <h1 style="margin: 0;">Lesson Planner – Theme # My Personal Goals for the Future Include... – Lesson # 3</h1>
    <p style="margin: 5px 0 0 0; font-size: 1.1em;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 3</p></td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Speaking</p></td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Grade:</b> 8th Grade (CEFR: A2.3)</p></td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Scenario:</b> Future Plans and Goals</p></td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Theme:</b> My Personal Goals for the Future Include...</p></td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</p></td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</p></td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Speaking: Productive: Discuss a recent learning experience. Interactive: Engage in discussions about academic and future professional interests.</p>
        </td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Speaking: Can explain a future learning experience by asking and responding to questions (e.g., "What will you be doing five years from now?" "I will be working as an engineer"). Can ask and answer questions about recent academic progress (e.g., "What did you learn this trimester?" "I improved my math skills"). Can explain academic goals by describing learning experiences in discussions (e.g., "I plan to take extra science classes next year").</p>
        </td>
    </tr>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276; text-align: center; margin-top: 20px;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead style="background-color: #f2f2f2;">
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task (Engagement, Modeling and Clarification)</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">This stage initiates the lesson by engaging students, activating prior knowledge, and introducing the topic of "Future Plans and Goals." The teacher models target language and clarifies key concepts for the upcoming speaking activities.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> Students watch a short 1-minute video clip (or look at a picture collage) showing young people engaging in various professions (e.g., engineer, doctor, artist, entrepreneur). The teacher asks, "What are these people doing? What do you think their <b>goals</b> were when they were your age?" and "What is your biggest <b>vision</b> for your <b>future</b>?" Students quickly share their initial ideas with a partner. (5 minutes)</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher writes "My future goals include..." on the board. The teacher models sentences like: "My future <b>goals</b> include studying medicine. I <b>plan to</b> be a doctor. I <b>have to</b> study hard for many years." The teacher emphasizes the pronunciation of "future," "goals," and the /θ/ sound in "math" (if applicable) and /s/ in "mass" as part of a general check. (3 minutes)</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"If I say, 'My goal is to finish high school,' is that a plan for yesterday, today, or the <b>future</b>?" (Expected answer: The future.)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"When I say 'I <b>have to</b> study,' does it mean it's optional or necessary?" (Expected answer: Necessary.)</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">The teacher clarifies any vocabulary from previous lessons that might be forgotten, such as "<b>career</b>," "<b>opportunity</b>," or "<b>ambitious</b>." (2 minutes)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Date: ___</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Time: 10 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 2 — Presentation</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Students receive new language input relevant to discussing future plans, building on the theme and scenario. This stage focuses on providing clear examples of target grammar and vocabulary in context through an authentic-like dialogue.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Input of new language/content connected to Scenario:</b> Students listen to or read a short dialogue (provided by the teacher) between two 8th-grade friends, Carlos and Ana, discussing their academic and <b>career goals</b> for after high school. (5 minutes)</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> Dialogue for an interview/casual conversation. Register: informal; Format: written text projected on screen or printed handout.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Dialogue example:</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Carlos: "Hey Ana, what are your <b>plans</b> for next year? What will you be doing?"</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Ana: "I <b>plan to</b> take extra science classes. In five years, I <b>will be working</b> as an environmental engineer, I hope! I <b>have to</b> get good grades this trimester."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Carlos: "That’s an <b>ambitious goal</b>! I learned a lot in <b>math</b> last trimester. I <b>want to</b> start my own <b>business</b>. Maybe I <b>will be studying</b> economics."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Ana: "That’s a great <b>vision</b>! You <b>must prepare</b> carefully. Remember, 'You <b>have to work hard</b> to <b>achieve</b> your <b>goals</b>.'"</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Engage in discussions about academic and future professional interests, using specific phrases for discussing goals and offering encouragement.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b> Students answer true/false questions based on the dialogue. (3 minutes)</p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Ana plans to take art classes next year. (True/False)"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Carlos wants to start his own <b>business</b>. (True/False)"</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Date: ___</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Time: 8 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">This stage focuses on building accuracy in speaking through controlled and semi-controlled practice of the target grammar and vocabulary. Activities progress from guided sentence formation to interactive exchanges, preparing students for fluent production.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Accuracy focus on Speaking.</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Using modals of necessity ("have to," "must"), WH-questions for goals, future continuous ("will be + -ing"), and vocabulary related to "future," "goals," "plan," "business," "career," "opportunity," "vision," "development," "ambitious," "important," "future-oriented," "plan," "achieve," "prepare," "set." Pronunciation focus on future tense structures and minimal pairs /θ/ and /s/.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Activity 1: Sentence Builder (Controlled Practice).</b> Students complete sentences orally using target vocabulary and grammar. Teacher provides sentence beginnings and options. Example: "In five years, I <b>will be</b> _______ (study/studying) ____ (business/career)." Students must choose the correct form and a relevant word. Teacher monitors pronunciation of "-ing" endings and modals. (5 minutes)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Activity 2: Chain Drill (Semi-Controlled Practice).</b> Students sit in a circle. The first student states a goal using "I <b>want to</b>..." or "I <b>plan to</b>...", e.g., "I <b>want to achieve</b> my dream of becoming a chef." The next student repeats the previous student's sentence and adds their own using a modal of necessity or future continuous, e.g., "Ana <b>wants to achieve</b> her dream of becoming a chef. I <b>have to</b> study English very hard." The teacher ensures correct use of "<b>have to</b>," "<b>must</b>," and future continuous, offering feedback on pronunciation, especially for "math" vs "mass" if words containing these sounds arise. (5 minutes)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Activity 3: Quick Questions (Pair Interaction).</b> In pairs, students take turns asking and answering WH-questions about recent academic progress and future goals. Example questions: "What did you learn in <b>math</b>/English last trimester?" "What <b>opportunity</b> do you want to create for yourself next year?" "What <b>development</b> do you foresee in your future studies?" They should also try to use "I <b>will be</b>..." for future plans. (5 minutes)</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Date: ___</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Time: 15 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">In this stage, students use the language freely and communicatively in a realistic scenario related to "Future Plans and Goals." The focus is on fluency, interaction, and completing a meaningful task.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative task: "Future Goals Interview."</b> Students work in new pairs. One student plays the role of an "interviewer" from a career development office, and the other is an "interviewee" (an 8th-grade student). The interviewer asks questions about the interviewee's academic progress, future learning experiences, and <b>career goals</b>. The interviewee responds by describing their <b>plans</b>, <b>vision</b>, and what they <b>will be doing</b> in the next 1, 3, or 5 years. (7 minutes per role, 14 minutes total)</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connect directly to Theme:</b> "My Personal Goals for the Future Include..." and <b>Scenario:</b> "Future Plans and Goals."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Students <b>must</b> use at least two phrases with "I <b>plan to</b>," two with "I <b>have to</b>/<b>must</b>," and two sentences with the future continuous ("I <b>will be working</b> as...," "I <b>will be studying</b>..."). They should also use at least three vocabulary words from the list (e.g., "<b>ambitious</b>," "<b>opportunity</b>," "<b>development</b>"). Interviewers should offer encouragement using phrases like "You <b>have to work hard to achieve</b> your <b>goals</b>!" (Sociolinguistic and Pragmatic competence).</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">After the interview, students briefly share one interesting thing they learned about their partner's <b>future plans</b> with the whole class.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Date: ___</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Time: 14 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">This stage involves formative assessment to check students' speaking abilities and application of target language. It also includes an opportunity for students to reflect on their own learning and performance.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative assessment strategy:</b> Teacher observation checklist during the "Future Goals Interview" task.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Students perform the "Future Goals Interview" role-play in pairs. The teacher circulates, observing and noting student participation, accuracy, and fluency.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Intelligible pronunciation of future tense structures and modals.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Appropriate use of target vocabulary (e.g., "<b>future</b>," "<b>goals</b>," "<b>plan</b>," "<b>career</b>," "<b>ambitious</b>").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Correct use of "<b>have to</b>," "<b>must</b>," "I <b>want to</b>," "I <b>plan to</b>," and future continuous (e.g., "I <b>will be working</b>").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Clarity in discussing recent learning experiences and future academic/professional interests.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Active listening and collaborative interaction with their partner (sociolinguistic competence).</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students complete an exit ticket with the following prompts:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"One thing I feel confident discussing about my <b>future plans</b> is..."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"One question I still <b>have</b> about talking about <b>future goals</b> is..."</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Date: ___</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Time: 8 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 6 — Reflection</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">This final stage encourages both students and the teacher to reflect on the lesson's effectiveness, identify areas for improvement, and bridge to the next lesson in the sequence.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student self-reflection prompt:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What part of today's speaking activities helped you the most in expressing your <b>future goals</b>?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What did you find challenging when asking or responding to questions about <b>future plans</b>, and what strategy could help you next time?"</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher reflection:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What worked well in helping students discuss their future plans and goals (e.g., specific activities, models, peer interaction)? The "Future Goals Interview" seemed to encourage more fluent use of the future continuous and modals.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What adjustments or additional scaffolds are needed for the next lesson to reinforce speaking skills or address common errors (e.g., more practice with WH-questions, clearer distinction between "have to" and "must" in specific contexts)? I noticed some students struggled with spontaneous question formation and using "will be -ing" consistently. I need to prepare more sentence frames for the next speaking task.</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson in the theme sequence:</b> Today, students practiced speaking about their future plans. In Lesson 4, we will transition to writing compositions, where students will write a short paragraph describing their personal <b>goals</b> and <b>vision</b> for the <b>future</b>, building on the vocabulary and grammatical structures practiced orally today.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Date: ___</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Time: 5 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>